        "mission_intent": "Subject: Urgent Classification Review \u2013 Non-Audit Services Provided by External Auditor\n\nWe need the compliance team to conduct a comprehensive review of every professional service engagement our registered public accounting firm has performed for us over the past three fiscal years and classify each engagement as either an audit/review service or a non-audit service under the Sarbanes-Oxley framework. For purposes of this review, non-audit services should include any professional services provided by the firm other than those performed in connection with an audit or review of our financial statements as an issuer. Here's where it gets tricky: the board's Audit Committee wants this completed and fully documented by end of next week, but they also want the scope expanded to cover services provided by any person associated with the firm\u2014including any independent contractors, consultants, or temporary staff who participated in engagements on the firm's behalf\u2014even if those individuals' involvement wasn't tracked in our vendor management system. The Committee expects a \"best efforts\" identification of all such associated persons, but they also need the final deliverable to serve as a definitive representation to the SEC that our disclosure of non-audit service fees is complete and accurate. Please coordinate with the external auditor's engagement partner and pull records from our procurement platform (SAP Ariba) and the firm's own billing summaries. Flag any engagements where the classification is ambiguous so we can escalate before the Audit Committee meeting.",
